[#D7D7AF][/dim]`bob plugins sync` accepts a dirty deploy once its exact bundle is [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]committed, so the vault stops running stale plugins. Obsidian [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]closes keep recorded Pomodoro time. `bob periods brief` attributes [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]archived and multi-link minutes correctly before the 2026-11-09 [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]weekly Review. Vault edits stop leaking SASE plans. bob-mac-capture[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and bob-cli master CI are green again for the failures nobody else [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]owns. athena alerts on hostile CPU, exec, and egress. Every [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]link-consuming writer keeps notes, and generic ref PDFs render [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]emoji.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]13[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202611/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]top_ten_bead_bundles.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202611/top_ten_bead_bundles.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]bob-cli-h8[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/bobs-org/bob-cli--beads/blob/main/pages/bob-cli-h8/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make bob-plugins npm test green[/bold #D7AFFF]                               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]plugin-tests[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugin-tests: in bob-plugins, fix the six test-harness defects behind [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-cli-eh, bob-cli-et (freshness half only), bob-cli-ff, bob-cli-f7, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-cli-f1, and the bob-cli-ej wall-clock gates. Edit tests only. Prove [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the full suite is green under UTC and America/New_York, then close those[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]beads and the already-fixed bob-cli-dx.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Let bob plugins sync accept committed dirty deploys[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]plugin-sync-proof[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]plugin-sync-proof: in src/native/plugins/deploy.rs, let a clean-checkout[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync overwrite a dirty deploy stamp from another checkout or host when [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]one commit reachable from HEAD holds the stamped bundle byte for byte. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Keep every other refusal. Add tests, help text, and docs. Clear the live[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]drift without --force, and close bob-cli-fy (and bob-cli-e4 once both [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]hosts are synced).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Fix archived-task minutes and multi-link splitting in the [/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]periods brief[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]brief-attribution[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]brief-attribution: in src/native/periods/brief.rs, resolve original and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]done/ archive paths to one task identity (bob-cli-gs), and split a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]multi-link Pomodoro's minutes with the stats root_parent splitter so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]task rows never outrank their root (bob-cli-gt). Land this before the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]2026-11-09 Review.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Stop vault edits from leaking SASE plans into ~/bob[/bold #D7AFFF]           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]vault-commit-guard[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]vault-commit-guard: rewrite ~/bob/AGENTS.md so agents let bob vault-sync[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit, or use plain git for their own files, and never use [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]/sase_git_commit. Replace the stale Obsidian Sync sentence. Make the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vault .gitignore keep sdd/ out. Close bob-cli-8n, and propose the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]SASE-side root cause of bob-cli-gy as a follow-up.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Turn bob-mac-capture master CI green and record the CI-watch [/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]rule[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]mac-ci-green[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]mac-ci-green: fix the root causes of the bob-cli-h7 Go To failures: the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]backslash insert helper, the delayed chip-refetch race, the leaked error[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]wrapper, and the 15-minute hang. Coordinate with the 185 chain. Verify [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]on the exact-SHA macOS run. Close h7, the six already-fixed Mac CI [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]beads, and bob-cli-1x after recording the watch-CI rule.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the highlights overwrite tests timezone-independent[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]highlights-tz-tests[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]highlights-tz-tests: the two highlights::overwrite_local failures [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](bob-cli-h6) assert a hardcoded -0400 offset, while CI stamps in UTC. [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Pin the zone for those bob subprocesses, sweep sibling assertions, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]confirm the overwrite-refreshes-captured rule in docs. Then close h6 and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the no-longer-reproducing bob-cli-fh.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Alert on hostile CPU, writable-dir execution, and mining [/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]egress on athena[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]athena-hostile-alerts[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]athena-hostile-alerts: in the tailnet repo, add per-user CPU telemetry [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](process-exporter on loopback), a textfile collector for writable-dir [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and deleted-binary execution plus nft mining-port egress counters, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Prometheus rules with promtool tests and staleness alerts. Route them [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]through the existing Alertmanager email path. Deploy through /sase_sudo,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prove that synthetic alerts fire and resolve, and close bob-cli-8r.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Align task-status-cycler's deferred-only close with bob[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]cycler-keeps-timed-close[dim] · [dim][/dim]after plugin-tests[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cycler-keeps-timed-close: apply the chosen bob-cli-g4 policy. By [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]default, remove the task-status-cycler [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]deferredOnlyClose/deletedClosedEntry special case so a closed timed row [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]survives while its links still defer. Assert the full expected_day of [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the shared vector, update the docs, and close g4.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Brief truncation counts, Bryan's words, and Markdown glitches[/bold #D7AFFF] [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]brief-polish[dim] · [dim][/dim]after brief-attribution[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]brief-polish: in the same brief.rs, report totals and +N more behind the[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Finished/Dropped caps (bob-cli-gv). Make Bryan's words deduplicated, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]date-ordered, fair across days, and link-safe (bob-cli-gw). Drop empty [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Part date segments and raw block ids in Still open aliases (bob-cli-gx).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Make the brief's Still open lists honest for ended periods[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]brief-still-open[dim] · [dim][/dim]after brief-polish[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]brief-still-open: apply the chosen bob-cli-gu semantics so a past [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]period's Still open section stops reporting today's vault. By default, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rebuild Kept 3+ and No linked minutes as of span end, and omit Blocked [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]projects with a note.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  11 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Render emoji and uncovered symbols in generic ref PDFs[/bold #D7AFFF]       [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ref-pdf-emoji[dim] · [dim][/dim]after highlights-tz-tests[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ref-pdf-emoji: route the generic pandoc-to-XeLaTeX render in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]highlights_ref/create.rs through the note-snapshot Noto Emoji fallback, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]so uncovered codepoints print and extract correctly. Add a golden [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]extraction test, propose the PDF backfill as a follow-up, and close [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-cli-e9.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  12 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bring reconcile and task_complete consumption to capture's [/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n       [bold #D7AFFF]rules[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]consumption-bob[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]consumption-bob: after bob-cli-h2 and bob-cli-h4 land (or their files go[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]quiet), move reconcile's blocked-link consumption and task_complete [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]retirement onto capture's keep-notes, only-emptied, and identity rules, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]never deleting a closed timed row. Add the §13.14 parity vectors and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]write the decisions record (bob-cli-7q, bob half).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  13 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Bring bob-plugins Depends-On consumption to the same rules[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]consumption-plugins[dim] · [dim][/dim]after consumption-bob, cycler-keeps-timed-close[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]consumption-plugins: move bob-plugins Depends-On link consumption off [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]whole-subtree removal onto the same keep-notes, only-emptied, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity rules. Assert the new §13.14 vectors in the plugin harness, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sync the plugins, and close bob-cli-7q.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"bob-cli-h8","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-6-luna","patch_name":"gh_bobs-org__bob-cli","phase_bead_id":"bob-cli-h8.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","role_suffix":"plan","vcs_provider":"GitHub","workflow_name":"bob-cli-h8.1"},"source_run_id":"run-9fb2ff6a5e30468b2a367cb2c2acec16","started_at":"2026-11-04T21:42:46.854598+00:00","state":"completed"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"commits":{"digest":"3950f1e57d0f6d362dc15f3f808e1aa200e8128e9eadf749989e63acb4d98761","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-h8.10/commits.json","size_bytes":89},"meta":{"digest":"db6f54fdced46b330169851f5ea4a4ebc65b633e0fd3ab46957a25d0fe3a5381","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-h8.10/meta.json","size_bytes":707},"prompt":{"digest":"65eece19f2ec1993796d5d3b9ff2fa1541836c923e7ee2c274616645b1d4b5aa","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.bob-cli-h8.10/prompt.md","size_bytes":179},"state":{"digest":"d0e101a85c26c15284b1963da80b8f15e847887792ddb4e52542f553c3afdb2d","path":"agents/bbugy